\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Paired comparison versus inherited safe improvement in all sixteen representation--risk cells. The left panel displays the complete-cost ratio P/L from the primary 64-state cohort and each of the three matched 32-state process clocks. Its range connects observed clocks and is not a confidence interval. The right panel displays the independently reconstructed sample mean original-policy contrast $J_L-J_P$ in $10^{-6}$ original-cost units; positive values favor P. These are numerical enclosures on the common sample, not population confidence intervals. Every cell is included; nine contrasts are exact zero and the other seven contain zero. Exact rational values, all clocks, plotting code and figure hashes are retained with the source.}}{42}{figure.0.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pairedlegacy120}{{1}{42}{Paired comparison versus inherited safe improvement in all sixteen representation--risk cells. The left panel displays the complete-cost ratio P/L from the primary 64-state cohort and each of the three matched 32-state process clocks. Its range connects observed clocks and is not a confidence interval. The right panel displays the independently reconstructed sample mean original-policy contrast $J_L-J_P$ in $10^{-6}$ original-cost units; positive values favor P. These are numerical enclosures on the common sample, not population confidence intervals. Every cell is included; nine contrasts are exact zero and the other seven contain zero. Exact rational values, all clocks, plotting code and figure hashes are retained with the source}{figure.0.1}{}}
